          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How do the picks work together?</h3>

          <p>
            Think of the list as parts of a system. The four panels store nothing, so on their own they only work while the sun is up, and they do their best work feeding a battery. The Anker 335 has no solar of its own, so it is useless without a panel or an outlet. Put a panel and the 335 together and each covers the other’s gap, which is why that pairing is the default recommendation in the buying section near the end of this guide.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Why is weight not listed?</h3>

          <p>
            We left weight out on purpose, because published figures vary between versions and listings and we would rather skip a number than print one we cannot stand behind. As a general rule, the fabric 21W panels are the lightest way to carry real solar capacity, the Nomad and BioLite give up some weight in exchange for a rigid stand, and a 20,000mAh bank weighs more than any of the panels.
